Vocalise — SVM Experiment 5
============================

Experiment:
Addition of Spectral Contrast features

Dataset:
CREMA-D
Total recordings: 7,442
Actors: 91
Classes: 6

Evaluation:
Speaker-independent train/test split
Test samples: 1,552
No actor overlap between train and test
Standardization: Training data only

Features:
13 MFCC means
13 MFCC standard deviations
ZCR mean/std
RMS energy mean/std
Spectral centroid mean/std
Spectral bandwidth mean/std
Spectral rolloff mean/std
Pitch/F0 mean/std
7 Spectral Contrast means
7 Spectral Contrast standard deviations

Total ML features: 52

Model:
SVM with RBF kernel

Results:
Accuracy: 52.0619%
Macro F1: 0.52

Class F1:
Angry:   0.70
Disgust: 0.41
Fear:    0.46
Happy:   0.46
Neutral: 0.49
Sad:     0.57

Confusion Matrix:
[[195, 23, 10, 27,  9,  1],
 [ 35,104, 13, 44, 24, 45],
 [ 24, 14,109, 37, 19, 62],
 [ 35, 33, 32,122, 30, 13],
 [  2, 41, 18, 27,111, 28],
 [  3, 31, 23,  9, 32,167]]

Comparison:
32 features: 48.26%
36 features: 48.84%
38 features: 50.1933%
62 features (+Chroma): 48.5180%
52 features (+Spectral Contrast): 52.0619%

Observation:
Adding spectral contrast increased accuracy from 50.1933%
to 52.0619% and Macro F1 from 0.50 to 0.52.

Spectral contrast therefore showed a positive contribution
to speaker-independent emotion classification in this experiment.